schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-mermaid-03-teaching-exploration-widget
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: kino-mermaid
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: teaching-exploration-widget
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook educator. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.Mermaid. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Teach Mermaid through runnable diagrams and concise comments.
  text: |-
    Create a Kino.Mermaid teaching and exploration cell that renders several small diagrams from local data: one flowchart, one sequence diagram, and one ER or state diagram. Use heredocs for static examples and an Elixir function that builds one diagram from a list of maps. Include comments explaining first-line type tokens, newlines, quoted labels, classDef styling, and why Kino.Mermaid output is static SVG.

    Requirements: include Livebook compatibility comments, accessible text summaries, fallback notes for old Kino versions, and safe execution checks. Do not rely on remote Mermaid libraries unless the fallback Kino.JS example is clearly optional and guarded. Sanitize or quote labels derived from data.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-mermaid-teaching-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino and renders multiple Kino.Mermaid.new/1 examples."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino and static SVG rendering."
  - "Reactive state: examples explain that changing the source data requires rerunning or regenerating the diagram."
  - "Data shape: static heredoc sources and data-driven records are documented with sanitized labels."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: each diagram has a concise text summary and old-version fallback notes."
  - "Safe execution: no eval, shell commands, credentials, unguarded remote libraries, or unsafe unquoted labels."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "Each Mermaid source starts correctly and uses real newlines."
    - "The code is valid and renders through Kino.Mermaid.new/1."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Teaches at least three Mermaid diagram types and a data-generated diagram."
    - "Explains core Mermaid and Kino.Mermaid constraints accurately in comments."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Examples are small enough to read and compare in one notebook flow."
    - "Text summaries and labels make each diagram understandable."
    - "Styling is consistent and avoids color-only meaning."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles unsafe labels, duplicate ids, empty data, and unsupported diagram choices."
    - "Keeps examples deterministic and bounded."
    - "Documents fallback paths without making them mandatory."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.Mermaid-centered and teaches through working Livebook diagrams."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-mermaid
- teaching-exploration-widget

